"[npm](https://www.npmjs.com/):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:15
msgid "Then, `require` it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:21
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:23
msgid "This module exports a single function named `rewritePattern`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:25
msgid "`rewritePattern(pattern, flags, options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:27
msgid ""
"This function takes a string that represents a regular expression pattern"
" as well as a string representing its flags, and returns an "
"ES5-compatible version of the pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:40
msgid ""
"_regexpu-core_ can rewrite non-ES6 regular expressions too, which is "
"useful to demonstrate how their behavior changes once the `u` and `i` "
"flags are added:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:52
msgid "The optional `options` argument recognizes the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:54
msgid "Stable regular expression features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:56
msgid ""
"These options can be set to `false` or `'transform'`. When using "
"`'transform'`, the corresponding features are compiled to older syntax "
"that can run in older browsers. When using `false` (the default), they "
"are not compiled and they can be relied upon to compile more modern "
"features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:58
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`unicodeFlag` - The `u` flag, enabling support for Unicode code point "
"escapes in the form `\\u{...}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:72
msgid ""
"`dotAllFlag` - The [`s` (`dotAll`) flag](https://github.com/mathiasbynens"
"/es-regexp-dotall-flag)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:91
msgid ""
"`unicodePropertyEscapes` - [Unicode property escapes](property-"
"escapes.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"By default they are compiled to Unicode code point escapes of the form "
"`\\u{...}`. If the `unicodeFlag` option is set to `'transform'` they "
"often result in larger output, although there are cases (such as "
"`\\p{Lu}`) where it actually _decreases_ the output size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:108
msgid ""
"`namedGroups` - [Named capture groups](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-"
"regexp-named-groups)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:117
msgid ""
"`unicodeSetsFlag` - [The `v` (`unicodeSets`) "
"flag](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-regexp-set-notation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:126
msgid ""
"By default, patterns with the `v` flag are transformed to patterns with "
"the `u` flag. If you want to downlevel them more you can set the "
"`unicodeFlag: 'transform'` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:143
msgid ""
"`modifiers` - [Inline `i`/`m`/`s` modifiers](https://github.com/tc39"
"/proposal-regexp-modifiers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:152
msgid "Experimental regular expression features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:154
msgid ""
"These options can be set to `false`, `'parse'` and `'transform'`. When "
"using `'transform'`, the corresponding features are compiled to older "
"syntax that can run in older browsers. When using `'parse'`, they are "
"parsed and left as-is in the output pattern. When using `false` (the "
"default), they result in a syntax error if used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:156
msgid ""
"Once these features become stable (when the proposals are accepted as "
"part of ECMAScript), they will be parsed by default and thus `'parse'` "
"will behave like `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:158
msgid "Miscellaneous options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:160
msgid "`onNamedGroup`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:162
msgid ""
"This option is a function that gets called when a named capture group is "
"found. It receives two parameters: the name of the group, and its index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:174
msgid "`onNewFlags`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:176
msgid ""
"This option is a function that gets called to pass the flags that the "
"resulting pattern must be interpreted with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:188
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:190
msgid ""
"[Lookbehind assertions](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-regexp-"
"lookbehind) cannot be transformed to older syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/regexpu-core_README.md:191
msgid ""
"When using `namedGroups: 'transform'`, _regexpu-core_ only takes care of "
"the _syntax_: you will still need a runtime wrapper around the regular "
"expression to populate the `.groups` property of "
"`RegExp.prototype.match()`'s result. If you are using _regexpu-core_ via "
"Babel, it's handled automatically."
msgstr ""

